# Optional: the stack runs without a .env. Compose reads this file only, to fill
# in docker-compose.yml. The stack's secrets (the credential encryption key, the
# internal RPC secret and every datastore password) are generated into volumes
# on the first start (README.md "Secrets"); application settings (LLM provider,
# SMTP, any other variable in docs/configuration.md) go in app.env, see
# app.env.example.

# Only during a GRAPH_SECRET_KEY rotation: the previous key(s), comma-separated,
# trusted for decryption only. Steps in deploy/README.md ("Rotating
# GRAPH_SECRET_KEY"); clear it again afterwards.
# GRAPH_RETIRED_SECRET_KEYS=

# Only with docker-compose.release.yml, which runs a published image instead
# of building this checkout (README.md "Running a published release"). The
# release workflow publishes one to ghcr.io/vulngraph/vulngraph for every
# release tag CHANGELOG.md lists. GRAPH_VERSION has no default: set it to such
# a tag (v0.1.0), optionally pinned to a digest (v0.1.0@sha256:<digest>), or to
# "edge", the rolling main-branch build with no upgrade guarantees. GRAPH_IMAGE
# runs a fork's published image.
# GRAPH_VERSION=
# GRAPH_IMAGE=ghcr.io/vulngraph/vulngraph
# COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml:docker-compose.release.yml
